IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sgta-nouns`
IMPORT `sgta-s2-definitions`
IMPORT `sgta-s11-approval`
IMPORT `sgta-part6-offences`
IMPORT `sgta-part8-penalties`
IMPORT `sgta-part9-general`

-- LAYER-1 TESTS: Part 6 offences (ss 53-59, 64, 71), s 11, the penalty end of Part 8 (ss 84-88) and ss 95, 96, 98.
-- Expected values are written by hand from the text of the Act (TA1999.txt).  The equipment is a walkie-talkie, a wired
-- telephone and a GPS receiver; the tests say what each section says and name no person's situation.
-- Argument order of a call is the order of the GIVEN of the rule (see the rule).

§ `Test equipment and holdings`

`a walkie-talkie` MEANS `A piece of equipment` OF "a hand-held walkie-talkie", (LIST `transmission`, `reception`), (LIST `Hertzian or radio waves`)
`a wired telephone` MEANS `A piece of equipment` OF "a wired telephone", (LIST `transmission`, `reception`), (LIST `wire`)
`a GPS receiver` MEANS `A piece of equipment` OF "a GPS receiver", (LIST `reception`), (LIST `Hertzian or radio waves`)

`holds nothing` MEANS `What the person holds` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`holds a section 5 licence` MEANS `What the person holds` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`holds a regulatory authorisation` MEANS `What the person holds` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`holds a Minister's exemption` MEANS `What the person holds` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`holds a treaty licence` MEANS `What the person holds` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`holds a Broadcasting Act licence` MEANS `What the person holds` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE

`the general penalty` MEANS `Penalty` OF 10000, 36, 1000, TRUE

§ `s 53 Unlawful operation of telecommunication system or service`

-- argument order: act, within Singapore, holds a s 5 licence, licence suspended under s 10, otherwise infringes the s 3 privilege, s 4 applies
#ASSERT `s 53(1): the person is guilty of an offence` `establishing` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 53(1): the person is guilty of an offence` `installing` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 53(1): the person is guilty of an offence` `maintaining` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 53(1): the person is guilty of an offence` `providing` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 53(1): the person is guilty of an offence` `operating` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- the five named verbs only; "using" and "selling" are in s 3(2)(a) but not in the verbs of s 53(1)
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 53(1): the person is guilty of an offence` `using` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 53(1): the person is guilty of an offence` `selling` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- the closing words: any act that otherwise infringes the privilege
#ASSERT `s 53(1): the person is guilty of an offence` `using` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- a licence under s 5 that is not suspended is a defence to the first limb; a suspended one is not
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 53(1): the person is guilty of an offence` `operating` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT `s 53(1): the person is guilty of an offence` `operating` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- outside Singapore the first limb does not bite
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 53(1): the person is guilty of an offence` `operating` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- "subject to this section and section 4"
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 53(1): the person is guilty of an offence` `operating` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT `s 53(2): the penalty` EQUALS `Penalty` OF 100000, 36, 10000, FALSE
#ASSERT `s 53(5): this other person is guilty of the offence` TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 53(5): this other person is guilty of the offence` FALSE))
#ASSERT `s 53(6): the defence is made out` TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 53(6): the defence is made out` FALSE))

§ `s 54 Prohibitions in respect of telecommunication and radio-communication equipment`

-- argument order: equipment, possesses it, what the person holds
#ASSERT `s 54(1)(b): the person contravenes` `a walkie-talkie` TRUE `holds nothing`
#ASSERT `s 54(1)(b): the person contravenes` `a GPS receiver` TRUE `holds nothing`
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 54(1)(b): the person contravenes` `a wired telephone` TRUE `holds nothing`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 54(1)(b): the person contravenes` `a walkie-talkie` FALSE `holds nothing`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 54(1)(b): the person contravenes` `a walkie-talkie` TRUE `holds a section 5 licence`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 54(1)(b): the person contravenes` `a walkie-talkie` TRUE `holds a regulatory authorisation`))
-- the exception names only a s 5 licence and regulations; exemption and treaty licence are in ss 56 and 96, not in s 54(1)
#ASSERT `s 54(1)(b): the person contravenes` `a walkie-talkie` TRUE `holds a Minister's exemption`
#ASSERT `s 54(1)(b): the person contravenes` `a walkie-talkie` TRUE `holds a treaty licence`
-- argument order: equipment, offers for sale / sells / possesses for sale it, what the person holds
#ASSERT `s 54(1)(a): the person contravenes` `a wired telephone` TRUE `holds nothing`
#ASSERT `s 54(1)(a): the person contravenes` `a walkie-talkie` TRUE `holds nothing`
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 54(1)(a): the person contravenes` `a wired telephone` TRUE `holds a section 5 licence`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 54(1)(a): the person contravenes` `a wired telephone` FALSE `holds nothing`))
#ASSERT `s 54(1): the person holds the licence or regulatory authority the exception names` `holds a section 5 licence`
#ASSERT `s 54(1): the person holds the licence or regulatory authority the exception names` `holds a regulatory authorisation`
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 54(1): the person holds the licence or regulatory authority the exception names` `holds nothing`))
-- s 54(2) outcome.  argument order: equipment, offers for sale, possesses, holds, "regulation of a system required for broadcasting", is broadcasting apparatus
#ASSERT `s 54(2): the outcome, on Reading A of s 95` `a walkie-talkie` FALSE TRUE `holds nothing` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `an offence under` OF "section 54(2)", `the general penalty`
#ASSERT `s 54(2): the outcome, on Reading A of s 95` `a walkie-talkie` FALSE TRUE `holds a section 5 licence` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no offence under this provision`
#ASSERT `s 54(2): the outcome, on Reading A of s 95` `a walkie-talkie` FALSE TRUE `holds a Minister's exemption` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no offence under this provision`
#ASSERT `s 54(2): the outcome, on Reading A of s 95` `a walkie-talkie` FALSE TRUE `holds a treaty licence` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no offence under this provision`
#ASSERT `s 54(2): the outcome, on Reading A of s 95` `a wired telephone` FALSE TRUE `holds nothing` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no offence under this provision`
-- FORK 3: for broadcasting apparatus the two readings differ, and only there
#ASSERT `s 54(2): the outcome, on Reading A of s 95` `a walkie-talkie` FALSE TRUE `holds nothing` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no offence under this provision`
#ASSERT `s 54(2): the outcome, on Reading B of s 95` `a walkie-talkie` FALSE TRUE `holds nothing` EQUALS `an offence under` OF "section 54(2)", `the general penalty`
#ASSERT `s 54(2): the outcome, on Reading B of s 95` `a walkie-talkie` FALSE TRUE `holds a section 5 licence` EQUALS `no offence under this provision`
-- the exceptions in s 95 itself: regulation of a system required for broadcasting is not excluded
#ASSERT `s 54(2): the outcome, on Reading A of s 95` `a walkie-talkie` FALSE TRUE `holds nothing` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `an offence under` OF "section 54(2)", `the general penalty`

§ `s 55 Penalty for unlicensed station`

-- argument order: equipment, establishes/installs/maintains/provides/operates it, where it is, what the person holds
#ASSERT `s 55(1): the person is guilty of an offence` `a walkie-talkie` TRUE `in a place in Singapore` `holds nothing`
#ASSERT `s 55(1): the person is guilty of an offence` `a walkie-talkie` TRUE `in a vehicle in Singapore` `holds nothing`
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 55(1): the person is guilty of an offence` `a walkie-talkie` TRUE `in a place in Singapore` `holds a section 5 licence`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 55(1): the person is guilty of an offence` `a walkie-talkie` TRUE `in a place in Singapore` `holds a regulatory authorisation`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 55(1): the person is guilty of an offence` `a walkie-talkie` TRUE `in a place in Singapore` `holds a Minister's exemption`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 55(1): the person is guilty of an offence` `a walkie-talkie` TRUE `in a place in Singapore` `holds a treaty licence`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 55(1): the person is guilty of an offence` `a wired telephone` TRUE `in a place in Singapore` `holds nothing`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 55(1): the person is guilty of an offence` `a walkie-talkie` FALSE `in a place in Singapore` `holds nothing`))
-- (2) possession is deemed operation until the contrary is proved
#ASSERT `s 55(2): the person is deemed to have operated it` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 55(2): the person is deemed to have operated it` TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 55(2): the person is deemed to have operated it` FALSE FALSE))
-- (3) the occupier; (4) the defence needs both limbs
#ASSERT `s 55(3): the occupier is guilty of an offence` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 55(3): the occupier is guilty of an offence` TRUE TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 55(3): the occupier is guilty of an offence` FALSE TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 55(3): the occupier is guilty of an offence` TRUE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT `s 55(4): the defence is made out` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 55(4): the defence is made out` TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 55(4): the defence is made out` FALSE TRUE))

